{"title": "Backoiler Spillfish", "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"druid-infobox druid-container noexcerpt\" id=\"druid-container-1\"><div><div class=\"druid-title\">Backoiler Spillfish</div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div class=\"druid-main-image\"><div class=\"druid-main-images-labels druid-tabs\"><div class=\"druid-main-images-label druid-tab druid-toggleable druid-title-tab focused\" data-druid=\"1-1\" data-druid-tab-key=\"In-Game\">In-Game</div></div><a href=\"/wiki/File:Backoiler_Spillfish.jpg\" class=\"image\"><img alt=\"Backoiler Spillfish.jpg\" src=\"/images/thumb/Backoiler_Spillfish.jpg/250px-Backoiler_Spillfish.jpg?b5766c\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"141\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/Backoiler_Spillfish.jpg/375px-Backoiler_Spillfish.jpg?b5766c 1.5x, /images/thumb/Backoiler_Spillfish.jpg/500px-Backoiler_Spillfish.jpg?b5766c 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div data-druid-section=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-section druid-section-Information\">Information</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-VariantOf\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-VariantOf\">Variant Of</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-VariantOf druid-data-nonempty\">\nBackwater Gunkfish</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-InternalID\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-InternalID\">Internal ID</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-InternalID druid-data-nonempty\">\nOilyStingray</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-MaxCount\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-MaxCount\">Max Count</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-MaxCount druid-data-nonempty\">\n6</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-PowerLevel\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-PowerLevel\">Power Level</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-PowerLevel druid-data-nonempty\">\n0.5</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-CauseofDeath\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-CauseofDeath\">Cause of Death</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-CauseofDeath druid-data-nonempty\">\nN/A</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-IsBodyRecoverable\" data-druid-section-row=\"Information\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-IsBodyRecoverable\">Is Body Recoverable?</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-IsBodyRecoverable druid-data-nonempty\">\nN/A</div></div></div><div class=\"druid-section-container\"><div data-druid-section=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-section druid-section-Stats\">Stats</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-Health\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-Health\">Health</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-Health druid-data-nonempty\">\n4</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-Damage\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-Damage\">Damage</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-Damage druid-data-nonempty\">\n0</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-DoorSpeedMultiplier\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-DoorSpeedMultiplier\">Door Speed Multiplier</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-DoorSpeedMultiplier druid-data-nonempty\">\n0.8</div></div><div class=\"druid-row druid-row-StunTimeMultiplier\" data-druid-section-row=\"Stats\"><div class=\"druid-label druid-label-StunTimeMultiplier\">Stun Time Multiplier</div><div class=\"druid-data druid-data-StunTimeMultiplier druid-data-nonempty\">\n1</div></div></div></div>\n<p>The <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> is a docile entity and variant of the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://lethal.miraheze.org/wiki/Backwater_Gunkfish\">Backwater Gunkfish</a> added by <b>Wesley's Ememy Variants</b>. It is a purple stingray with two small eyes, five tentacles for its mouth, and a dark green coloration around its eyes, on its back, and on its stinger.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Mechanics\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Mechanics\">&gt; Mechanics</span></h2>\n<p>Similar to the Backwater Gunkfish, the <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> will find a location to enter its hiding state near scrap, at an AI node, or near the closest player and can be heard flopping around while it does so. If any player enters its line of sight while it moves to this location, it will immediately stop moving and enter its hiding state.\n</p><p>After entering its hiding state, the <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> will remain there indefinitely if no players are in the interior or on the exterior where it is. If players are in the interior or on the exterior where it is, it will instead check for nearby players on a timer. If this timer runs out, it will get up, leave a small puddle of oily goo behind, and find a new location to hide.\n</p><p>If a player steps on, hits, or remains too close to a <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> for too long, it will be frightened and spray all nearby players with goo that covers their hud. It will then flee, leaving behind a trail of slippery and oily goo that lasts for the rest of the day.\n</p><p>Two universal bugs exist for the Backwater Gunkfish and all its variants. Firstly, all of them practically have 5hp instead of 4hp, as they only die after their hp drops below 0 rather than at 0. Secondly, all of them will use the same goo as whichever one first sprayed goo on a moon. For example, the <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> will use the same goo as the <a href=\"/wiki/Springwater_Hotfish\" title=\"Springwater Hotfish\"><b>Springwater Hotfish</b></a> if the latter sprayed goo first, making the <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> capable of killing players. However, these are mostly just auditory or visual differences.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Spawn_Chances\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Spawn_Chances\">&gt; Spawn Chances</span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> only has a chance to spawn within the interiors of <a href=\"/wiki/Oldred\" title=\"Oldred\"><b>Oldred</b></a> (25.97%) and <a href=\"/wiki/Thalasso\" title=\"Thalasso\"><b>Thalasso</b></a> (9.80%). \n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Bestiary_Entry\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Bestiary_Entry\">&gt; Bestiary Entry</span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> has the same entry as the Backwater Gunkfish.\n</p>\n<table class=\"article-table mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Backwater Gunkfish <span style=\"padding-left:0.5em;\">&#x2060;</span>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<table style=\"border: 15px solid #8E8E83; font-size: 135%; font-family: Tomorrow; color: #01A801; border-spacing: 0px;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"padding: 25px; background-color: #151515;\">Backwater Gunkfish<br /><br />Sigurd's danger level: 0% but these little goopy goblins wont leave me ALONE<br /><br />Scientific name: Infectum linteum<br /><br />The Backwater Gunkfish is a type of Gunkfish of the family Mobulidae. Unlike the other types of Gunkfish, the Backwater Gunkfish spends most of its time on land. It can inhabit any damp, warm space where a water source is present. Its body is fat, flat, squishy and gelatinous, the width of a doormat. Its tail, slightly harder than the rest of its soft body, can range from 2-3 feet in length. When stressed, its tail is often curled up over its head to position for firing mucus or to shake and rattle as a deterrent.<br /><br />The Backwater Gunkfish feeds off organic material on surfaces, and for this reason, it is found most often around polluted water, swamps, or dirty sewers. When frightened, the Gunkfish can use an opening in its tail to release a burst of a thick, green mucus mixed with saliva to defend itself; the Backwater Gunkfish keeps an especially large \"reserve\" for emergency situations and can squirt multiple times. When needed, it uses part of this extra reserve to excrete from its body, increasing its mobility on land.<br /><br />The Backwater Gunkfish is harmless and is considered a natural cleaner of its preferred environments. Its mucus is a disinfectant; though it is not safe or healthy to consume, it is unlikely to cause major harm if it enters the body through the eyes or nose. Its smell is often described as a mix of vinegar and lard, and it is slightly warm when freshly excreted.<br /><br />Though not directly harmful, the Backwater Gunkfish is often considered a notorious pest to water treatment facilities and petroleum refineries. The gunkfish itself is evasive, capable of fitting itself into very small holes and pipes, and its mucus is arduous to remove once it has hardened, forming a substance comparable to ice. For all these reasons, the Backwater Gunkfish has lead to many accidents and should be taken seriously. Today, pest removal services are well-accustomed to safe Gunkfish removal and relocation operations, and there are many affordable options if you believe there is one in the area. The best way to prevent a Gunkfish infestation is to keep your environment clean and dry and to close off any access to standing water.\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Audio\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Audio\">&gt; Audio</span></h2>\n<div class=\"noresize\">\n<table class=\"wikitable sortable mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" style=\"text-align: center;\" data-expandtext=\"\u25bc\" data-collapsetext=\"\u25b2\">\n<caption style=\"white-space: nowrap;\">Audio\n</caption>\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Action</th>\n<th>Sound\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Flopping</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"8\" data-mwtitle=\"StingrayFloppingNoVocals.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/StingrayFloppingNoVocals.mp3?aa9b0f\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/StingrayFloppingNoVocals.mp3/StingrayFloppingNoVocals.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sting</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"2\" data-mwtitle=\"OilyStingraySting.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/OilyStingraySting.mp3?fb5118\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/OilyStingraySting.mp3/OilyStingraySting.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Spitting</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"3\" data-mwtitle=\"OilyStingraySpitLong.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/OilyStingraySpitLong.mp3?66133c\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/OilyStingraySpitLong.mp3/OilyStingraySpitLong.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Goo</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"3\" data-mwtitle=\"OilyStabPoison.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/OilyStabPoison.mp3?dff537\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/OilyStabPoison.mp3/OilyStabPoison.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sliding</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"11\" data-mwtitle=\"OilyStingraySlide.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/OilyStingraySlide.mp3?43f828\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/OilyStingraySlide.mp3/OilyStingraySlide.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Whining</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"6\" data-mwtitle=\"StingrayWhining2.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/StingrayWhining2.mp3?212c36\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/StingrayWhining2.mp3/StingrayWhining2.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dying</td>\n<td><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"2\" data-mwtitle=\"StingrayDie.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/StingrayDie.mp3?944f16\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/StingrayDie.mp3/StingrayDie.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Trivia\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Trivia\">&gt; Trivia</span></h2>\n<p>While the <b>Backoiler Spillfish</b> uses the same flopping sound effect as the Backwater Gunkfish in-game, it does have a unique flopping sound effect with the unused vocals from the vanilla game.<br /><audio controls=\"\" preload=\"none\" width=\"320\" style=\"width:320px;max-width:100%;max-height:100%\" data-durationhint=\"9\" data-mwtitle=\"OilyStingRayFlopping.mp3\" data-mwprovider=\"local\"><source src=\"/images/OilyStingRayFlopping.mp3?ea5b97\" type=\"audio/mpeg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /><source src=\"/images/transcoded/OilyStingRayFlopping.mp3/OilyStingRayFlopping.mp3.ogg\" type=\"audio/ogg; codecs=&quot;vorbis&quot;\" data-transcodekey=\"ogg\" data-width=\"0\" data-height=\"0\" /></audio>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\".3E_Gallery\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"&gt;_Gallery\">&gt; Gallery</span></h2>\n<ul class=\"gallery mw-gallery-traditional\">\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:BackoilerSpillfishFleeing.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"The Backoiler Spillfish fleeing and leaving its goo behind.\"><img alt=\"The Backoiler Spillfish fleeing and leaving its goo behind.\" src=\"/images/thumb/BackoilerSpillfishFleeing.jpg/120px-BackoilerSpillfishFleeing.jpg?5a9cd6\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/BackoilerSpillfishFleeing.jpg/180px-BackoilerSpillfishFleeing.jpg?5a9cd6 1.5x, /images/thumb/BackoilerSpillfishFleeing.jpg/240px-BackoilerSpillfishFleeing.jpg?5a9cd6 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">The Backoiler Spillfish fleeing and leaving its goo behind.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n\t\t<li class=\"gallerybox\" style=\"width: 155px\"><div style=\"width: 155px\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"thumb\" style=\"width: 150px;\"><div style=\"margin:16px auto;\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:BackoilerSpillfishCorpse.jpg\" class=\"image\" title=\"The corpse of the Backoiler Spillfish.\"><img alt=\"The corpse of the Backoiler Spillfish.\" src=\"/images/thumb/BackoilerSpillfishCorpse.jpg/120px-BackoilerSpillfishCorpse.jpg?270dfe\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"120\" height=\"68\" srcset=\"/images/thumb/BackoilerSpillfishCorpse.jpg/180px-BackoilerSpillfishCorpse.jpg?270dfe 1.5x, /images/thumb/BackoilerSpillfishCorpse.jpg/240px-BackoilerSpillfishCorpse.jpg?270dfe 2x\" data-file-width=\"1920\" data-file-height=\"1080\" /></a></div></div>\n\t\t\t<div class=\"gallerytext\">The corpse of the Backoiler Spillfish.</div>\n\t\t</div></li>\n</ul></div>", "images": ["Backoiler_Spillfish.jpg", "BackoilerSpillfishFleeing.jpg", "BackoilerSpillfishCorpse.jpg", "StingrayFloppingNoVocals.mp3", "OilyStingraySting.mp3", "OilyStingraySpitLong.mp3", "OilyStabPoison.mp3", "OilyStingraySlide.mp3", "StingrayWhining2.mp3", "StingrayDie.mp3", "OilyStingRayFlopping.mp3"], "cats": ["Pages_with_DRUID_infoboxes"]}